  descriptor for each (an IL node of kind 159, LIB_DSC) in the section
  libdsc, and in the section std_lib a pointer to each.  A DSEE derived
  object, built from std_lib.mac (a macro file: one entry per routine).

  Image addresses (DOMAIN C 6.9; the unit is in both binaries with no
  routines): its .blocks record names the module std_lib and
  stdlib_dummy (no block: not a routine; perhaps a variable of the
  generated source, or the macro's dummy).  Its file record lists:
    the code start  cc.m68k 0x0B3E9C, cc.a88k 0x0B2640 (inside cargs.pas's
                    code: the unit has none);
    A5              cc.m68k 0x19DB88, cc.a88k 0x31DBF8 (sortidntk.pas's:
                    no module data in .data);
    libdsc          cc.m68k 0x0ED4C0, cc.a88k 0x2B3ED8, 0x138C bytes (a
                    read-only section beside the code; the same bytes
                    in both binaries);
    std_lib         cc.m68k 0x2D2B68, cc.a88k 0x493514, 0x2DC bytes:
                    globals_from_backend.ins.pas's std_lib_rtns.
  The survey's 4488 and 6408 bytes are spans to the next unit.

  A descriptor (all 176 with +0 0 and +2 159): +4 a longword of
  register bits (the registers the call kills, by its use: 00FFFEFE
  for the integer routines, 00FCFCC0 / 00FCF800 for fpp_$, ...); +8 the
  name's length; +10 the number of arguments n; +12 n words, each
  argument's size (1 a word, 2 a longword; 9, 11 the vector routines'
  kinds); then the name, padded to a longword.  std_lib_rtns[k] (+4k) is
  the address of descriptor k (.rwdi, in descriptor order); +704..+731
